  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array AAA of NNN non-negative integers, we define f(A)f(A)f(A) in the following way:\n\n\nConsider all partitions of the array AAA into continuous subarrays, A[L1,R1],A[L2,R2],…,A[LK,RK]A[L_1, R_1], A[L_2, R_2], \\ldots, A[L_K, R_K]A[L1​,R1​],A[L2​,R2​],…,A[LK​,RK​] (you can choose KKK), where\n\n1≤Li≤Ri≤N1 \\le L_i \\le R_i \\le N1≤Li​≤Ri​≤N\nL1=1L_1 = 1L1​=1, RK=NR_K = NRK​=N\nRi=Li−1+1R_i = L_{i - 1} + 1Ri​=Li−1​+1\n\n\nThe score of a partition is defined as ∑i=1K(ALi∣ALi+1∣ALi+2∣…∣ARi)\\sum_{i = 1}^{K} (A_{L_i} | A_{L_i + 1} | A_{L_i + 2} | \\ldots | A_{R_i})∑i=1K​(ALi​​∣ALi​+1​∣ALi​+2​∣…∣ARi​​), where ∣|∣ represents the Bitwise OR operator.\nLess formally, the score is the sum of Bitwise ORs of all subarrays.\nA partition is called optimal if and only if it has the minimum possible score over all partitions.\nf(A)f(A)f(A) is defined as the maximum possible KKK that can be used in an optimal partition.\nYou are given an array AAA of NNN non-negative integers.\n\nFind ∑L=1N∑R=LNf([AL,AL+1,AL+2,…,AR]\\sum_{L = 1}^{N} \\sum_{R = L}^{N} f([A_L, A_{L + 1}, A_{L + 2}, \\ldots, A_R]∑L=1N​∑R=LN​f([AL​,AL+1​,AL+2​,…,AR​], i.e. the sum of fff over all subarrays of AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the size of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the value of ∑L=1N∑R=LNf([AL,AL+1,AL+2,…,AR]\\sum_{L = 1}^{N} \\sum_{R = L}^{N} f([A_L, A_{L + 1}, A_{L + 2}, \\ldots, A_R]∑L=1N​∑R=LN​f([AL​,AL+1​,AL+2​,…,AR​].",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2300 \\le A_i \\lt 2^{30}0≤Ai​&lt;230",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
