    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n2\n1 2\n3\n2 1 3\n4\n5 5 2 2\n3\n0 0 0\n8\n0 2 7 8 0 4 1 2",
        "output": "4\n7\n14\n10\n72",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : There are 333 subarrays:\n\n[1][1][1] : Only one possible division, which is trivially optimal. It has K=1K = 1K=1.\n[2][2][2] : Only one possible division, which is trivially optimal. It has K=1K = 1K=1.\n[1,2][1, 2][1,2] : There are 222 possible divisions, one is [1,2][1, 2][1,2] and the other is [1]+[2][1] + [2][1]+[2]. Both are optimal, because both have a score of 333. Thus, the maximum KKK is 222.\n\nHence, the sum is 1+1+2=41 + 1 + 2 = 41+1+2=4."
      }
    ]
